<!--
  <sui-empty-state> — SUI port of <ship-empty-state>.
  Centered placeholder for empty lists / missing content with icon tile,
  typography, and action slot.

  Prop / event / method parity vs <ship-empty-state>
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Lit                          SUI                      Notes
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  variant ('default'|'inline'| variant (default|        ✓ SUI renames Lit's
    'placeholder'|'connecting') inline|placeholder|       'default' dashed-card
                                 connecting, 'default',   variant to 'default'
                                 reflect)                 (matches SUI naming);
                                                         'connecting' adds
                                                         aria-live=polite +
                                                         role=status
  size ('sm'|'md'|'lg',        size (sm|md|lg,          ✓
    'md')                        'md', reflect)
  tone (Tone, undefined)       tone (union, 'muted',     ✓ tints icon tile;
                                 reflect)                 muted default keeps
                                                         neutrals for bare states
  icon (String, '')            OMITTED                  Requires JS to look up
                                                         lucide-icons registry
                                                         and render fallback SVG;
                                                         template-only divergence.
                                                         Callers use slot="icon".
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  iconSlotFilled tracking →    reflect-empty=           ✓ SUI reflect-empty
    hide .icon tile when empty  "data-no-icon"           hides tile automatically
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  role=note / role=status      role on .box inner div   ✓
    + aria-live=polite           driven by variant prop
    for connecting variant
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  slots: icon, title, default  slots: icon, title,      ✓
    (desc), action               default (desc), action
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  parts: box, icon, title,     parts: box, icon,        ✓
    desc, actions                title, desc, actions
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from the feat/next baseline, parity-gate pass)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - No L1 controls here (the action slot's contents are caller-provided).
  - `:host { display: block; color: var(--muted-foreground) }` moved to the
    host-sx directive below; `font-family` has no sx keyword and stays a
    residual `:host{}` rule.
  - TONE: feat/next hardcoded the icon tile's background/ring to the static
    `--tone-default-bg`/`--tone-default-ring` tokens regardless of the actual
    [tone] value — only the glyph color (`--tone-fg`) varied per tone (via
    the framework's older, 3-channel tone contract). The new contracts.css
    ships a full 6-channel contract per tone (adds `--tone-bg`/`--tone-border`/
    `--tone-ring`), so the tile now reads `var(--tone-bg)`/`var(--tone-fg)`/
    `var(--tone-ring)` directly — background and ring now ALSO tint per tone
    (primary/info/success/warning/destructive/accent), not just the glyph.
    This is a deliberate, visible change from feat/next's look for those 6
    tones (closer to the prop's original intent); see the report for detail.
    The bare/default/muted exception block is kept verbatim — it encodes a
    genuine design choice (empty states read quiet/neutral by default) that
    the global tone='default' mapping (a translucent foreground tint) would
    not reproduce.
  - Dropped the local `--tone-fg: var(--muted-foreground)` fallback at plain
    `:host{}` — `tone` is a reflected prop with a default, so the host always
    carries a concrete `[tone]` value once mounted and the global contract
    always resolves; no local default needed.
  - SIZE: the six size-driven dimensions here (outer padding x/y, gap, icon
    glyph size, tile size, title/desc font sizes) have no global counterpart
    — the framework's `size-*` channels are a 4-value control contract
    (height/x-pad/font-size/gap) built for buttons/inputs, not a multi-axis
    block layout. Kept as component-scoped local custom properties
    (`--es-*`) set per `[size]` value, exactly as feat/next — not exposed via
    `sx` (an ad-hoc `sx` channel would be a LANG-GAP; a local `<style>`
    custom property consumed only inside this file's own residual CSS is
    not the same thing and isn't one).
  - `<sui-stack class="copy">` → `<column class="copy">`: `sui-stack` is
    retired (`crates/sui/lint/src/rules/legacy_layout.rs` maps it to
    `column`); no other markup changed. Dropped the now-redundant
    `.copy { min-width: 0 }` rule — `<column>`'s lowering already applies
    `min-width: 0` to itself and its direct children.
  - `.box`/`.icon`/`.actions` stay plain `<div>` (matches feat/next and
    sui-alert's own `.box`/`.ico`/`.actions` — raw `<div>` is still legal at
    this package's lint policy; not force-migrated to `<row>`/`<column>` as
    that's a separate, unrequested structural change).
  - Everything else (variant-conditional surface/typography, the icon tile's
    size/tone exceptions, `::slotted` rules, forced-colors) is unchanged from
    feat/next: still reads tokens only, and is either variant/size-conditional
    (not a single static value sx could hold) or has no sx keyword
    (text-align, flex-direction, margin-inline-start, line-height numerics).
-->

<prop name="variant" values="default|inline|placeholder|connecting" default="default" reflect />
<prop name="size" values="sm|md|lg" default="md" reflect />
<prop name="tone" values="default|primary|info|success|warning|destructive|accent|muted" default="default" reflect />

<host sx="display:block fg:muted-foreground"></host>

<style>
  :host {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    --es-pad-y: 64px;
    --es-pad-x: 16px;
    --es-gap: var(--space-3);
    --es-icon: 22px;
    --es-tile: 48px;
    --es-title-fs: var(--text-md);
    --es-desc-fs: var(--text-sm);
    --es-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    --es-border: 1px solid var(--border);
    --es-bg: var(--tone-muted-bg);
    --es-shadow: var(--shadow-xs);
  }

  :host([size='sm']) {
    --es-pad-y: var(--space-7);
    --es-pad-x: var(--space-4);
    --es-gap: var(--space-2);
    --es-icon: 16px; --es-tile: 36px;
    --es-title-fs: var(--text-base);
  }
  :host([size='lg']) {
    --es-pad-y: 96px;
    --es-pad-x: var(--space-6);
    --es-gap: var(--space-4);
    --es-icon: 28px; --es-tile: 64px;
    --es-title-fs: var(--text-lg);
    --es-desc-fs: var(--text-base);
  }

  :host([variant='placeholder']),
  :host([variant='connecting']) {
    --es-border: 0;
    --es-bg: transparent;
    --es-radius: 0;
    --es-shadow: none;
    --es-pad-y: var(--space-6);
  }
  :host([variant='inline']) {
    --es-border: 1px dashed var(--border);
    --es-bg: var(--tone-muted-border);
    --es-radius: var(--radius-md);
    --es-pad-y: var(--space-3);
    --es-pad-x: var(--space-4);
    --es-gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .box {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--es-gap);
    padding: var(--es-pad-y) var(--es-pad-x);
    text-align: center;
    background: var(--es-bg);
    border: var(--es-border);
    border-radius: var(--es-radius);
    box-shadow: var(--es-shadow);
  }
  :host([variant='inline']) .box {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    text-align: start;
  }

  .icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: var(--es-tile);
    height: var(--es-tile);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--tone-bg);
    color: var(--tone-fg);
    line-height: 1;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--tone-ring);
  }
  :host(:not([tone])) .icon,
  :host([tone='default']) .icon,
  :host([tone='muted']) .icon {
    background: var(--muted);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }
  :host([data-no-icon]) .icon { display: none; }
  :host([variant='inline']) .icon {
    width: var(--es-icon);
    height: var(--es-icon);
    background: transparent;
    box-shadow: none;
  }
  ::slotted([slot='icon']) {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: currentColor;
  }
  ::slotted(svg[slot='icon']) {
    width: var(--es-icon);
    height: var(--es-icon);
  }

  .title {
    font-family: var(--heading-font);
    font-size: var(--es-title-fs);
    font-weight: var(--heading-weight);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
  }
  :host([variant='connecting']) .title,
  :host([variant='placeholder']) .title {
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .desc {
    font-size: var(--es-desc-fs);
    max-width: 38ch;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }
  :host([variant='inline']) .desc { max-width: 60ch; }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  :host([variant='inline']) .actions {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-inline-start: auto;
    justify-content: flex-end;
  }

  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .box { border-color: CanvasText; }
    .icon { background: Canvas; color: CanvasText; }
  }
</style>

<div class="box" part="box"
     role={variant() === 'connecting' ? 'status' : 'note'}
     aria-live={variant() === 'connecting' ? 'polite' : 'off'}>
  <div class="icon" part="icon" aria-hidden="true">
    <slot name="icon" reflect-empty="data-no-icon"></slot>
  </div>
  <column class="copy" gap="1" align={variant() === 'inline' ? 'start' : 'center'}>
    <div class="title" part="title"><slot name="title"></slot></div>
    <div class="desc" part="desc"><slot></slot></div>
  </column>
  <div class="actions" part="actions">
    <slot name="action"></slot>
  </div>
</div>
